  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 103.02 Action level",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 103.02 “Action level” means the concentration of lead or copper in water, determined in accordance with Env-Dw 714, which determines the treatment requirements that a water system is required to complete.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 100) #10606, eff 6-1-14",
